From fd77795e897183b7988a74b8b494576ddc65ea09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 08:00:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/dadao: implement maskable async dispatch core
 (KL-131a)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds SEE §5 steps 2-6 (nonmaskable bypass, inner_cfx_mask/global_cfx_mask/
excp_cause_mask arbitration, trap/sync/async counters) as a shared gate
(dadao_cfx_dispatch()) in front of KL-122a's precise-entry carrier
(dadao_cfx_precise_trap_enter(), steps 7-10). All three prior call sites
(cfx_smon CFXTRAP, cfx_ptw CFXTRAP-as-call, cfx_ptw/cfx_tlb fault delivery)
are nonmaskable and route through unchanged behaviorally except for the
new trap/sync counters.

New architectural registers: cg0-3/rc1 shared global_cfx_mask (one per
mode, not per cfxcode, per the wiki's explicit "shared register" note),
cg0-3/rc11 per-cfx/mode excp_cause_mask, cg5/rc63 RO excp_cause_nonmaskable
(hardware-static per cfx cause table), cg4/rc2-4 HW trap_num/excp_sync_num/
excp_async_num counters.

New instruction-boundary asynchronous dispatch: dadao_cpu_exec_interrupt()
now performs a real scan (dadao_cfx_async_step() -> dadao_cfx_async_scan())
implementing contracts/isa/spec.md §8.5.1's frozen priority rule (lowest
pending eligible cfxcode, then lowest eligible cause bit). CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD
is asserted unconditionally at reset (matching gem5's always-live
FullSystem interrupt polling) since a genuinely pending-and-newly-unmasked
cause can arise from plain guest cfx2rc writes alone, not just a test
source; only the max_insns=1 TB-forcing needed for true instruction-
boundary precision stays gated behind dadao_cfx_async_active() to avoid a
performance regression on the 99.9% case where nothing is pending.

Test-only additions (never guest-visible ABI): a synchronous dispatch
trigger (cg4/rc60) that lets a test program directly invoke the steps 2-6
gate with an arbitrary (target, cause, is_sync=true) triple -- needed
because M1's only real maskable synchronous cause (FPEXCP) has no
execution path (RF excluded from M1); two independent persistent
level-triggered async test sources (cfx-async-test-level-{a,b}-code/seed
CPU properties) driving the new instruction-boundary delivery probes.

dadao_cfx_dispatch() returns bool (entered vs blocked/pending-only) so
callers reached from mid-TB helper code can avoid an unconditional
cpu_loop_exit() re-fetching and re-executing the same instruction forever
on a blocked attempt -- a real bug this task's own self-review hit and
fixed in the TEST-ONLY trigger path.

Zero regression: KL-120a/122a/124a-129a probes, 81/81 lit E2E,
run_differential.py (AGREE(3-way)=200, AGREE(4-way)=200, zero DIVERGE),
manifest_check.py, check_issues.py all unchanged from baseline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
